WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:02.792
Imani and Rosa are planning a holiday.

00:03.201 --> 00:07.117
Imani wants to book early, but Rosa keeps asking for more time.

00:07.486 --> 00:12.805
Before giving a speech about indecision, Imani asks what Rosa still needs to decide.

00:13.201 --> 00:17.716
Rosa explains that food and transport may make the whole trip unaffordable.

00:18.099 --> 00:22.270
The issue was not choosing a destination, as Imani had imagined.

00:23.288 --> 00:26.719
Eyal and colleagues tested whether imagining another person’s

00:26.732 --> 00:28.582
perspective improved accuracy.

00:28.978 --> 00:32.983
Across twenty-five experiments, it did not consistently help.

00:33.391 --> 00:36.925
In a final experiment, talking to the person did help.

00:37.333 --> 00:41.172
That supports obtaining information rather than polishing a guess.

00:41.580 --> 00:46.402
It does not guarantee that every answer is complete or truthful, or require someone to

00:46.414 --> 00:48.034
disclose private matters.

00:49.080 --> 00:53.187
An open question invites someone to explain in their own words rather than

00:53.200 --> 00:54.718
simply answer yes or no.

00:55.127 --> 00:58.533
What is making the decision difficult leaves more room than why

00:58.545 --> 00:59.744
are you being difficult.

01:00.152 --> 01:05.267
After Rosa identifies cost, Imani can ask whether a total budget would help.

01:05.650 --> 01:10.038
Rosa can state what she can spend without revealing her income or debts.

01:11.080 --> 01:15.289
Imani could say: You like the idea, but food and transport might

01:15.302 --> 01:16.565
make it too expensive.

01:16.974 --> 01:18.811
Have I understood you correctly?

01:19.193 --> 01:21.221
Rosa can correct that account.

01:21.617 --> 01:25.775
So you want everyone to wait because you did not plan adds blame instead.

01:26.183 --> 01:30.048
Imani can explain her own worry directly: I am concerned that

01:30.061 --> 01:31.808
prices will rise if we wait.

01:32.830 --> 01:36.452
A leading question suggests the answer the questioner expects.

01:36.862 --> 01:41.300
Why did you break your promise is open, but it assumes a promise was broken.

01:41.709 --> 01:45.854
If the friends disagree about an earlier agreement, what do you remember us

01:45.867 --> 01:47.283
agreeing leaves more room.

01:47.678 --> 01:51.951
Separate the remembered words from what each person understood them to mean.

01:52.997 --> 01:58.111
Elizabeth Loftus reviewed research showing that misleading information after an event

01:58.124 --> 01:59.566
can affect later memory.

01:59.975 --> 02:04.146
That is a reason not to supply unverified details in questions.

02:04.528 --> 02:08.903
It does not prove a particular memory false or justify dismissing harm.

02:09.311 --> 02:12.615
Where an appropriate message exists, check it together.

02:13.023 --> 02:16.990
I would love to come may express interest rather than a booking commitment.

02:18.038 --> 02:22.426
The friends might disagree about what the hotel price includes, what waiting might

02:22.439 --> 02:24.556
cost, or what each person wants.

02:24.926 --> 02:27.184
Check the quote for included costs.

02:27.554 --> 02:30.411
Discuss uncertainty about later prices.

02:30.794 --> 02:33.065
Negotiate different preferences.

02:33.448 --> 02:37.504
Explaining the hotel bill cannot decide how much Rosa should spend.

02:37.886 --> 02:41.343
Each kind of disagreement calls for a different next step.

02:42.372 --> 02:46.313
Imani can explain a real deadline: I need to book by Friday.

02:46.683 --> 02:49.005
Could we compare the full costs tonight?

02:49.414 --> 02:53.138
If it does not fit your budget, I can book my trip and we can plan

02:53.151 --> 02:54.248
something else together.

02:54.643 --> 02:56.352
Rosa may still decline.

02:56.760 --> 03:01.595
Once she understands the options and answers, repeated questions aimed at changing her

03:01.607 --> 03:02.934
no can become pressure.

03:03.955 --> 03:09.159
After someone explains a concern, pause and ask: Have I understood you correctly?

03:09.543 --> 03:12.068
Let them correct you before giving your view.

03:12.464 --> 03:16.941
Afterwards, notice whether you learned something or merely secured agreement.

03:17.349 --> 03:21.239
If asking could lead to threats or harm, you do not have to continue.

03:21.608 --> 03:25.690
Better wording cannot make an unsafe relationship safe on its own.
